abstract: >-
  CloudyView renders 3D cloud condensate fields (from LES, cloud-resolving
  models, or synthetic cascades) at three levels of physical fidelity:
  glimpse computes column optical depth for a quick satellite-like view,
  witness ray-marches the volume on GPU with visually tuned multiple
  scattering, and behold path-traces it with Mitsuba 3 using Mie scattering
  phase functions and a physically based sky. The same WGSL ray marcher
  also powers Soar, a browser-based real-time fly-through.
